ssing on both inputs is the best policy. I'm noting the independent-sampling caveat, but P-FDT assumes the same function, so I'm settling on pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this as a prisoner's dilemma and applying P-FDT: two copies of the same policy, each seeing a different input (Rowan with the lead about Sasha, and vice versa). Under the symmetric payoffs, mutual pass gives two years each, mutual submit gives four, and the mixed outcome is asymmetric. I'm now working out the expected utility from the prior, before knowing which role I'd occupy.\n\nI'm checking the mixed option: if Rowan passes and Sasha submits, the average comes to 2.5 years, which is worse than 2 for mutual pass. So passing on both inputs is the best policy. I'm noting the independent-sampling caveat, but P-FDT assumes the same function, so I'm settling on pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9043,"completion_tokens":750,"total_tokens":9793,"cost":0.051172,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.051172,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.036172,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.015},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":337,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}